# Agent Anti-Patterns (learned from experience)

## Authentication — NEVER debug Keycloak for API testing

The ROS API uses `x-rh-identity` header (base64 JSON), NOT Bearer tokens.
Keycloak tokens are only used by the frontend OAuth proxy.

**Always use the forged identity:**
```bash
IDENTITY=$(echo -n '{"identity":{"account_number":"10001","org_id":"1234567","type":"User","user":{"username":"admin","email":"admin@example.com","is_org_admin":true}},"entitlements":{"cost_management":{"is_entitled":true}}}' | base64 -w0)
curl -H "x-rh-identity: $IDENTITY" http://localhost:8080/api/...
```

Do NOT attempt to:
- Get a Bearer token from Keycloak (it won't work alone)
- Debug `unauthorized_client` errors (the client is confidential by design)
- Discover client secrets (unnecessary — the header above bypasses everything)

## Cluster Connectivity — verify BEFORE attempting any operation

If `oc login` or `oc whoami` fails, STOP immediately and ask the user to:
1. Connect VPN
2. Start sshuttle: `sshuttle -r root@dell-r640-041.bkr.lab.eng.rdu2.dc.redhat.com 192.168.122.0/24`

Do NOT:
- Retry the same command hoping it will work
- Try SSH to the hypervisor (if oc fails, SSH will also fail — same network)
- Attempt alternative authentication methods

## Performance Testing — use Prometheus metrics, not log parsing

The processor has comprehensive Prometheus instrumentation:
- `rosocp_pipeline_phase_duration_seconds` — per-phase timing
- `rosocp_recommendation_duration_seconds` — per-type recommendation timing
- `rosocp_db_query_duration_seconds` — per-operation DB timing

Query these via `curl http://localhost:9000/metrics` rather than parsing log timestamps.

## Image Deployment — ALWAYS use unique tags

Never reuse image tags. `imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent` means Kubernetes won't pull
a new image with the same tag. Use `feature-$(date -u +%Y%m%d%H%M)` for unique tags.

## Project Structure Awareness

Key directories for AI agents:
- `docs/performance/` — Performance audit and profiling reports
- `docs/fedramp/` — FedRAMP compliance documentation
- `docs/security/` — Public-facing security docs (MkDocs site)
- `internal/ingestion/` — CSV parsing + digest computation (43% of pipeline time)
- `internal/engine/` — Recommendation generation (container=83% of recommend time)
- `internal/api/` — HTTP handlers (GORM reflection is the #1 API-side bottleneck)
- `internal/config/security.go` — Security enforcement (graduated model)
- `internal/metrics/` — Prometheus instrumentation definitions
